Ryujinx shader translator: allow 32 storage buffer slots per shader instead of 16 (_sbSlotWritten is a 32-bit mask already).
Some DKB compute shaders (e.g. 3d1ddc3fbb3d4afc) address 17 distinct global-memory pointers held in c[0]; with 16 slots the
17th failed with "Failed to reserve storage buffer for global memory operation". The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
Applied at build time by Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy under obj/patched; the staged checkout stays untouched.
--- a/Translation/ResourceManager.cs
+++ b/Translation/ResourceManager.cs
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
             _stagePrefix = GetShaderStagePrefix(stage);
 
             _cbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[18];
-            _sbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[16];
+            _sbSlotToBindingMap = new SetBindingPair[32];
             _cbSlotToBindingMap.AsSpan().Fill(new(-1, -1));
             _sbSlotToBindingMap.AsSpan().Fill(new(-1, -1));
 
